  "id": "COMPOUND:30029 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Cassialactone is shown to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the cell line FaDu. The first pathway links Cassialactone to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is targeted by 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone, a compound that in turn targets FaDu. The second pathway connects Cassialactone to Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is also targeted by the same chromone compound, again leading to FaDu. The third pathway shows Cassialactone targeting Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is targeted by a different compound that also targets FaDu. These findings suggest that Cassialactone may exert its effects through multiple distinct pathways, all of which converge on FaDu. The evidence supports a potential role for Cassialactone in modulating cellular processes that are relevant to FaDu, though the exact mechanisms by which these targets influence FaDu remain to be fully elucidated.",
